<section class="wrap rv split" style="align-items:start">
  <div>
    <p class="eyebrow">WHY EMBERTERM</p>
    <h2 class="h2">One job, done without drama.</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="body lead">
    <p>Terminals that forget your tabs, or fail to start after an update, cost you time every day. EmberTerm was written to replace one that did both.</p>
    <p>It keeps a single job: open fast, show your shells, and bring everything back the way you left it. Settings, profiles and the session are plain files you can read, and a broken file is set aside with a notice instead of blocking startup.</p>
  </div>
</section>
